              "id": "8fd18c50-b070-330b-a83a-f395a49bd524",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Prohibited C Function Identified\" vulnerability refers to the use of certain C library functions that are considered unsafe due to their potential to cause buffer overflows, format string vulnerabilities, or other types of security issues. In this case, the `qsort` function is not inherently unsafe, but it can lead to vulnerabilities if not used correctly.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use safer alternatives to these functions whenever possible. In the case of `qsort`, it is generally safe to use as long as the comparison function is implemented correctly. However, if the comparison function can lead to undefined behavior (for example, by not correctly handling the case where the two elements are equal), it can potentially lead to a security vulnerability.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe `qsort` function in your code seems to be used correctly. However, without seeing the implementation of `vx_uint8_compare`, it's hard to say for sure. Make sure that `vx_uint8_compare` handles all possible input cases correctly.\n\nHere is a simple example of a comparison function for `uint8_t` values that should be safe:\n\n```cpp\nint vx_uint8_compare(const void* a, const void* b) {\n    uint8_t arg1 = *reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t*>(a);\n    uint8_t arg2 = *reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t*>(b);\n\n    if(arg1 < arg2) return -1;\n    if(arg1 > arg2) return 1;\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `cstdlib` for `qsort`\n- `cstdint` for `uint8_t`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C++](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_SCP_v2.pdf)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS154189"
                ]
              }
